&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Old Mission is a global proprietary trading firm that leverages state-of-the-art technology and research to identify and execute profitable trading strategies across multiple asset classes around the world. Our offices in Chicago, New York, and London are all composed of naturally-curious individuals who thrive in a team environment and constantly strive for improvement.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Position&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking to hire a Floor Trader to join our expanding team on the CBOE (Chicago Board Options Exchange). After completing our comprehensive new-grad training program and working closely with experienced traders, this individual will transition to the trading floor, operating in an open outcry environment as part of a collaborative team using our proprietary pricing strategies. The ideal candidate is competitive, driven, and thrives in a fast-paced, team-oriented setting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for verbally executing trades and building out our floor footprint&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate effectively with our traders upstairs and other floor traders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for creating and maintaining relationships with floor brokers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to make quick decisions under stressful situations with incomplete information&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outgoing and easy to get along with&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving skills, attention to detail, and the ability to multi-task&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good Risk management skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Desire to win and constantly improve&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Superior organizational and communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;p-rich_text_section&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Benefits and Perks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;p-rich_text_list p-rich_text_list__bullet&quot; data-stringify-type=&quot;unordered-list&quot; data-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fully paid Medical, Dental, Vision, Disability, and Life Insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fully stocked kitchen; free breakfast and lunch every day on-site&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tuition Reimbursement Program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) with employer match&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid Vacation, Sick, and Parental leaves&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commuter and Flexible Spending Programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Base Salary Range&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;$80,000 - $100,000 - Salaries are based on numerous factors such as skills, experience, and education. Our compensation package also includes a discretionary bonus and a comprehensive benefits program for full-time employees. For more information, reach out to your recruiter.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Old Mission Capital is not accepting unsolicited resumes from any staffing/search firms. All resumes submitted by staffing/search firms to any employee at Old Mission Capital via-email, the Internet or directly without a valid signed search agreement will be deemed the sole property of Old Mission Capital, and no fee will be paid in the event the candidate is hired by Old Mission Capital.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Old Mission is not accepting unsolicited resumes from any staffing/search firms. All resumes submitted by staffing/search firms to any employee at Old Mission via-email, the Internet or directly without a valid signed search agreement will be deemed the sole property of Old Mission, and no fee will be paid in the event the candidate is hired by Old Mission.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Old Mission is a global proprietary trading firm that leverages state-of-the-art technology and research to identify and execute profitable trading strategies across multiple asset classes around the world. Our offices in Chicago, New York, and London are all composed of naturally-curious individuals who thrive in a team environment and constantly strive for improvement.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Position&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Old Mission is a proprietary quantitative trading firm and is currently recruiting a Fundamental Analyst to join the Options team in our Chicago headquarters. This research analyst will be responsible for conducting economic, event-driven, and company-specific research and analysis and will work with the team to discover new trading opportunities for the firm. We value idea generation over reporting. We are looking for someone who can stay up to the minute with breaking market events, use fundamental principles to interpret them quantitatively, and help influence trading decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and analyze financial/events/information that will have an impact on the options of underlying securities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support traders by being the sole point of contact for conducting quantitative and macroeconomic research&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze datasets to identify their potential impact on the price of certain securities and their underlying options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct quantitative and qualitative analysis on information that could affect trading decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate directly with traders by providing them with the fundamental overlay necessary to do many things, including developing tools, analyzing market data, and testing strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An undergraduate or an advanced degree in a quantitative field such as computer science, engineering, or one of the hard sciences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive knowledge of securities analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant analyst experience preferred, but not required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to think quantitatively, analyze, and clearly communicate in a time-sensitive trading environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient conducting research across domestic and international financial markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to multitask across many different projects, securities, and asset classes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Programming experience preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits and Perks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;p-rich_text_list p-rich_text_list__bullet&quot; data-stringify-type=&quot;unordered-list&quot; data-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Fully paid Medical, Dental, Vision, Disability, and Life Insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Fully stocked kitchen; free breakfast and lunch every day on-site&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Tuition Reimbursement Program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;401(k) with employer match&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Flexible Spending Plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Commuter Benefit Program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Base Salary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;$125,000 - Salaries are based on numerous factors such as skills, experience, and education. Our compensation package also includes a discretionary bonus and a comprehensive benefits program for full-time employees. For more information, reach out to your recruiter.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
