&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ready to do the most impactful work of your career? At&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/?utm_campaign=mt_o_m_w_m_m__coi_0_jd-onchain&amp;amp;utm_source=coinbase&quot;&gt;Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;, we are uncompromising on our mission to increase economic freedom. The bar is high, the environment is intense, and we like it that way. This isn&#39;t a place for complacency, it’s a place to be pushed past your perceived limits. If you&#39;re ready to build the future of finance alongside people who refuse to settle for &quot;good enough,&quot; you belong here. Coinbase is a remote-first, but not remote-only company. Expect to get together quarterly for intense in-person working sessions called “surges.”&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/careers&quot;&gt;learn more about working at Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;This is a 12-week internship during summer 2027.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Internal Audit Analytics Intern, you&#39;ll join the Internal Audit Data Analytics Team and support data-driven testing of controls across Coinbase&#39;s global technology infrastructure and crypto-native products. You&#39;ll extract, analyze, and validate datasets from Coinbase&#39;s internal data systems to assess control design and operational effectiveness, translating audit data requests into SQL-based extracts and actionable findings that support the audit team&#39;s control testing objectives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write SQL queries against Snowflake and other internal data platforms to assess the design and operational effectiveness of key internal controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building continuous auditing processes and AI tooling for use throughout Internal Audit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Test system and model changes by validating compliance and performance impact, and document results for relevant stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce data extracts and reports from a variety of sources, translating audit data requests into clear, actionable requirements and outputs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Validate data ETL processes from upstream production systems into the data repository and from the repository into enterprise tools, checking for completeness and accuracy at each stage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills and Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Currently pursuing a degree in Data Science, Computer Science, Statistics, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated SQL proficiency with experience writing queries and working with large datasets through coursework, projects, or prior internships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with data ETL concepts, including how data moves between production systems, repositories, and enterprise tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience presenting data findings to non-technical audiences through written reports, presentations, or project deliverables&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilizes generative AI responsibly, maintaining human oversight to deliver business-ready outputs and drive measurable improvements in workflow efficiency, cost, and quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
