&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;About Cubist:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cubist Systematic Strategies, an affiliate of Point72, deploys systematic, computer-driven trading strategies across multiple liquid asset classes, including equities, futures and foreign exchange. The core of our effort is rigorous research into a wide range of market anomalies, fueled by our unparalleled access to a wide range of publicly available data sources.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Role:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Quantitative Developer for a PM team focused on systematic credit and related asset classes. This is a unique opportunity to collaborate, learn, and lead technology projects with high business impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and develop software for strategy research and trading.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and improve tools for data acquisition, processing, and visualization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work on the execution/order management system, live dashboards, and P&amp;amp;L reconciliation tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the team’s CI/CD pipeline, job running infrastructure, and other tech components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure robustness and efficiency of the team’s systems. Be ready to troubleshoot and correct any issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with the portfolio manager, quant researchers, and traders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Requirements:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Undergraduate or graduate degree in Computer Science.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience developing research and trading infrastructure at a financial institution, or demonstrated excellent skills required for the role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience with execution/order management systems, real-time data servers, and visualization is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of Linux OS—system components, process management, shell scripting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Python, including in the object-oriented design, unit/reg testing, conda environment management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of SQL, JavaScript, Apache airflow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to take ownership of his/her work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commitment to the highest ethical standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Career with Point72’s Foundation and Community Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Steven &amp;amp; Alexandra Cohen Foundation is a nonprofit organization committed to inspiring philanthropy and community service, leading by example to show the world what giving can do. Working closely with the Foundation, the Office of Inclusion &amp;amp; Community is the engine that drives the philanthropic culture and strong sense of community among the employees of Point72, a global asset management company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the day‑to‑day accounting operations for a portfolio of private foundations and corporate community programs, including financial reporting, audit coordination, tax support, and account reconciliations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the month‑end and year‑end close processes across multiple private foundations, including preparation and posting of accruals and other journal entries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee fundraising and donation receivables, including tracking, recording, and reconciling related activity to ensure completeness and accuracy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform monthly financial reviews and reporting to validate the integrity of financial information and proper coding across entities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and review account reconciliations on a recurring basis to ensure accuracy across multiple legal entities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support state and federal tax reporting requirements, partnering with external tax preparers as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate and support the annual audit process, including preparation of schedules, responding to auditor inquiries, and addressing follow‑up items.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with banking relationships and ongoing cash management activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
